  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fair Finance Cambodia-CCC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fair Finance Coalition Cambodia (FFC) achieved remarkable result during the first phase. The coalition managed to build a good relationship with some key regulators of the banking sector for instant the National Bank of Cambodia, the Ministry of Economy and Finance. However, the challenge still exists in engaging individual banking institution and also private company for some research studies despite there was improvement made in the relationship in the capacity building area.

For this phase II from 2023-2024, CCC&#x2019;s plan to conduct policy dialogue on green financing policy in Cambodia&#x2019;s banking sector using the findings and policy recommendation from the research study on needed green financing policy for banking sector in Cambodia.
For phase 2, CCCwill contribute to the 5 result areas of the project. The following are the detailed key activities of project implementation plan of CCC.

Result Area 1 - Financial institutions (FIs) operating across the region increasingly adopt or improve sustainable finance policies, practices and public disclosure.

Key Activities:
&#x2022; Topic of study: Green Financing Policy
&#x2022; Theme: ESG
&#x2022; Area of focus (e.g. financial institutions covered, affected communities of focus, etc.): Banking Sector
&#x2022; Country/region covered: Cambodia
&#x2022; Potential collaboration with other FFA/FFI countries: Vietnam, Thailand
&#x2022; Lead organization for study: CCC

Please describe main knowledge products (e.g. bank policy assessments conducted /policy briefs for financial institutions developed), influencing and campaign efforts, and themes of interest for these (e.g. engagements with banks on green finance), as well as main changes to deliverables such as postponements to activities planned for 2023.

CCCC will complete two postponedactivities from 2022 - one is the research study on ADB&#x2019;s COVID-19 Post Pandemic Economic Recovery (final report, policy brief and the dissemination of the study report), and the other one is the establishment of the policy tracker on sustainable financepolicy and ESG related policy.

Result Area 2 - Regulators and governments increase independent monitoring of FI policy, practice and accountability and transparency, and improve the regulation of FIs, including through mandatory regulation.
Key Activities:

CCC will organize a half-day policy dialogue and prepare policy brief with policy maker, FI, NBC, ABC, and other regulators specifically focusing on finding and recommendation from green financing study and ESG related policy. This event will beorganized in collaboration with other FFC members and the total number of participants of around 50-60 people including guest speakers.

Result Area 3 - Regional financial sector actors take increasing actions to require and enforce improved standards for FIs&#x2019; policies, practices, accountability and transparency.

Key Activities:
CCC will join with other members of the FFC andalso FFA in advocating for green finance policy and ESG related policy through key regional platform for instant Indonesian coalition through ASEAN Engagement, C20 engagement. And if possible, the Indian coalition through G20.

Result Area 4 - Strong and resilient civil society across the region effectively influences the sustainable finance agenda across the region, integratinga gender lens and community voice.

Key Activities:
- -Attend training, follow up, mentoring and coaching
- Reporting about the progress of the training of FFC and FIs

Result Area 5 - Other actors (intermediary stakeholders) have increased awareness and take increased action to influence the sustainable finance agenda.

Key Activities:
- CCC could use its e-communication channels i.e. Facebook page, Website, Twitter to communicate infographic of research study and other achievements in order tobuild visibility of FFC as well as its NGOmembers.</narrative>
  </description>
